# Local development configuration. Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and fill in.
# Only the server reads this file, and only outside production. Variables already
# present in the environment always win, so Replit/CI settings override the file.
#
# Everything below is portable application configuration unless a comment says
# otherwise. Replit-provided variables are listed at the end and are only ever
# read as fallbacks — never add a real bucket id, hostname or credential here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PostgreSQL connection for local development (see docs/development/local-setup.md
# for the Docker command). The only database setting: no separate host, user or
# password variables exist. A hosted URL may carry `?sslmode=require`.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://vault:change-me@localhost:5432/vault_dev

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HTTP
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local HTTP port. Replit sets PORT=5000 itself; macOS reserves 5000, so 5001 locally.
PORT=5001

# Hostnames this deployment serves, comma-separated and bare (no scheme). Required in
# production; the preferred, portable setting in every environment. Locally, loopback is
# always allowed; list any extra development hostnames here.
# VAULT_ALLOWED_HOSTS=vault.example.com

# debug | info (default) | warn | error. Events below the level are dropped.
# LOG_LEVEL=info

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# File storage
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where file bytes live. `local` is a directory (development, tests, or a host with a
# persistent volume). `replit` is Replit App Storage. Production must set this
# explicitly: a deployment filesystem is not durable.
VAULT_STORAGE_PROVIDER=local

# `local` only: the directory holding object bytes.
VAULT_STORAGE_LOCAL_DIR=.vault-data/files

# Required whenever VAULT_STORAGE_PROVIDER is not `local`: the bucket this deployment
# owns. It names the storage INSTANCE, and is what keeps a development deployment from
# writing into production's store. Supplied per environment as a secret in the host;
# never commit a real bucket id.
# VAULT_STORAGE_BUCKET=replace-with-the-bucket-for-this-environment

# Optional key prefix inside the bucket (`dev`, `production`, `vault/production`).
# Slash-separated segments of letters, digits, dot, underscore or hyphen, each starting
# with a letter or digit. A second line of defence, not a substitute for separate buckets.
# VAULT_STORAGE_PREFIX=dev

# Maximum accepted upload, in bytes. Default 50 MiB.
# VAULT_MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES=52428800

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# First-admin bootstrap
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used only by `npm run bootstrap:admin`, once. Remove the password line after the
# first successful run. Never set these on a web server.
# VAULT_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_EMAIL=you@example.com
# VAULT_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD=replace-with-at-least-12-characters
# VAULT_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_NAME=Your Name

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Replit-provided (never set by hand; read only as fallbacks)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REPLIT_DOMAINS     the deployment's hostnames. Used as the production host list when
#                    VAULT_ALLOWED_HOSTS is unset, and allowed outside production too.
# REPLIT_DEV_DOMAIN  the workspace preview host; allowed outside production.
# PORT               set by the platform.
#
# Prefer VAULT_ALLOWED_HOSTS in both environments: it is explicit and portable.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test harness only
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VAULT_REPLIT_LIVE_STORAGE_BUCKET  a DEVELOPMENT App Storage bucket, set only to run
#                                   tests/storage/replit-file-storage.live.test.ts inside
#                                   a Replit workspace. Never the production bucket.
